            {
              "endIndex": 13658,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 13658,
                    "startIndex": 13565,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Dell CEO Michael Dell sees memory demand explosion at Bank of America event on April 7, 2026\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 13565
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 13659,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 13659,
                    "startIndex": 13658,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 13658
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 14212,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 14212,
                    "startIndex": 13659,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "“I would say memory in advanced silicon, it’s kind of the 25 times 25. And what do I mean by that? So when NVIDIA came out with the H100, it had 80 gigabytes of high bandwidth memory. The current part has 288 gigabytes. Next year, you’ll hear about parts with 1 terabyte. And the year after that, you’ll hear about parts with 2 terabytes. So from 80 gig to 2 terabytes is 25 times more memory per accelerator. And in that timeframe, you’ll have about 25 times more accelerators. So 25 times 25 is 625 times. I know most of you are pretty good at math.”\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 13659
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 14858,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 14858,
                    "startIndex": 14212,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "“And it also takes about four years to build a new memory plant, assuming you don’t have shells already built. And if you wanted to have memory capacity in 2027, you would have made the investments in 2023. If we dial back the clock to 2023, you might recall it was a horrible year for semiconductors, particularly memory. Micron, in particular, had negative gross margin percentage. Their sales went in half from 2022 to 2023, and the industry collectively lost $40 billion. A lot of them still have PTSD from that. And they’re like scared little puppies. Some of them almost went bankrupt. And so they’re sort of very careful about investing.”\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 14212
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 14859,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 14859,
                    "startIndex": 14858,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 14858
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 14908,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 14908,
                    "startIndex": 14859,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Google CEO Sundar Pichai on Cheeky Pints podcast\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 14859
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 15118,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 15118,
                    "startIndex": 14908,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "“Memory is definitely one of the most critical components now.” “There is no way the leading memory companies are going to dramatically improve their capacity. So you have those constraints in the short term.”\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 14908
            },
