                      "content": "Niall Ferguson -\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 1698
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 1716,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 1716,
                    "startIndex": 1715,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 1715
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 1940,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 1940,
                    "startIndex": 1716,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "For the habitual critics of U.S. foreign policy in general and Donald Trump’s in particular, the analogy between today’s air raids against Iran and the invasion of Iraq nearly 23 years ago is too obvious to be resisted. 1/9\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 1716
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 1941,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 1941,
                    "startIndex": 1940,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 1940
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 2293,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 2293,
                    "startIndex": 1941,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "However, Iran 2026 is not Iraq 2003. Regime alteration is not regime change. It rules out the deployment of American ground forces other than special forces. It requires a short time frame for military operations. It will disappoint those who want to fast-track Iran (and Venezuela) to democracy. But the lesson of Iraq has not been lost on Trump. 2/9\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 1941
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 2294,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 2294,
                    "startIndex": 2293,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 2293
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 2657,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 2657,
                    "startIndex": 2294,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Yes, Iran can lash out and is lashing out, firing missiles at Israel and at U.S. bases in the Gulf region. Yes, the Iranians may try to replay 1973 and 1979 by causing an oil price shock. And yes, it is a lot to expect the Iranian people to rise up against a regime that just weeks ago had the ruthlessness to slaughter protesters in their tens of thousands. 3/9\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 2294
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 2658,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 2658,
                    "startIndex": 2657,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 2657
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 2923,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 2923,
                    "startIndex": 2658,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "But Operation Epic Fury differs from Operation Iraqi Freedom. The goal is not to march into Iran and confer, much less impose, freedom on the Iranians. It is to decapitate the Islamic Republic’s political structure and leave the Iranians to take their freedom. 4/9\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 2658
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 2924,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 2924,
                    "startIndex": 2923,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 2923
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 3216,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 3216,
                    "startIndex": 2924,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Will this succeed? We don’t yet know, but it’s important to note that the Iranian regime has few effective friends. Moreover, Iran’s barrage of missile attacks on its neighbors’ territory has achieved little other than to convert fence-sitters into supporters of the U.S.-Israeli effort. 5/9\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 2924
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 3217,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 3217,
                    "startIndex": 3216,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 3216
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 3363,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 3363,
                    "startIndex": 3217,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The real question is: Who rules in Tehran after Khamenei? Or, to put it bluntly, who’s the Iranian Delcy Rodriguez in this regime alteration? 6/9\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 3217
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 3364,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 3364,
                    "startIndex": 3363,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 3363
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 3609,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 3609,
                    "startIndex": 3364,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The biggest risk lies outside the Middle East. It remains that of a Taiwan Crisis, the economic consequences of which would be greater than the 1973-74 Oil Shock because of the centrality of Taiwan’s semiconductor fabs to the world economy. 7/9\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 3364
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 3610,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 3610,
                    "startIndex": 3609,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 3609
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 3817,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 3817,
                    "startIndex": 3610,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Détente with China will not be easy if Venezuela—not to mention Cuba and parts of Mexico—has descended into chaos, peace is nowhere in sight in Ukraine, and a new war is still raging in the Middle East. 8/9\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
