                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 17845
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 18145,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 18145,
                    "startIndex": 17894,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Near-consensus: The single flat loop wins over complex orchestration. File system as extended memory. Errors preserved, not cleaned. Fake planning tools (TodoWrite, todo.md) for coherence. Primitives (bash, grep, filesystem) over custom integrations.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 17894
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 18406,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 18406,
                    "startIndex": 18145,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Active disagreement: How to handle tool overload. Manus uses logit masking (all tools loaded, constrain outputs). Cursor uses lazy loading (load tool definitions on demand). Opposite strategies. Both work. The right answer might depend on your token economics.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 18145
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 18751,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 18751,
                    "startIndex": 18406,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Active disagreement: How much should the harness manage for the model? Google's bet is \"give the model everything, let it figure it out\" (2M token windows). Everyone else builds harnesses that actively filter and stage information. Research still shows 15-47% performance drops as input grows. The harness-heavy approach is winning in practice.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 18406
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 19007,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 19007,
                    "startIndex": 18751,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Unsolved: How to evaluate harness quality. Cursor's 46.9% token reduction is one of very few published numbers. No standard benchmarks exist for comparing harness designs head-to-head. When to share sub-agent state vs isolate it is still purely empirical.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 18751
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 19324,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 19324,
                    "startIndex": 19007,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The pattern worth noting: The teams shipping the best agents keep simplifying. Manus: five rewrites, each one removed things. Anthropic designs Claude Code's scaffold to shrink as models improve. Replit went from one agent to three but each individual agent got simpler. Over-engineering is the default failure mode.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 19007
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 19367,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 19367,
                    "startIndex": 19324,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "What This Means If You Are Building Agents\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 19324
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 19407,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 19407,
                    "startIndex": 19367,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Three things this research makes clear:\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 19367
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 19476,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 19476,
                    "startIndex": 19407,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Spend your engineering cycles on the harness, not on model shopping.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 19407
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 19538,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 19538,
                    "startIndex": 19476,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Progressive disclosure is not optional, it is architectural. \n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 19476
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 19595,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 19595,
                    "startIndex": 19538,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Plan for your harness to get simpler, not more complex. \n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 19538
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 19956,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 19956,
                    "startIndex": 19595,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Dex Horthy (creator of the \"12 Factor Agents\" methodology) puts the threshold at 40% of the model's input capacity: push past that and you enter what he calls the \"dumb zone\" - signal-to-noise degrades, attention fragments, and agents start making mistakes that look like reasoning failures but are actually information overload from a poorly designed harness.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 19595
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 19990,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 19990,
                    "startIndex": 19956,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Source: Horthy \"12 Factor Agents\"\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 19956
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 20062,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 20062,
                    "startIndex": 19990,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The model is the engine. The harness is the car. Nobody buys an engine.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 19990
            },
