                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 23768
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 24375,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 24375,
                    "startIndex": 23769,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Two weeks ago I made a bet with Vitalik that one person could agentic-code an Ethereum client targeting the entire 2030+ roadmap. Completed-roadmap Ethereum is a genuinely extraordinary machine - 10,000+ TPS on L1, finality in seconds instead of 15 minutes, solo staking for 1 ETH, stateless nodes on a $7 Raspberry Pi, over a million TPS across L1+L2 - but that future depends on 65 planned upgrades across eight phases actually fitting together. The specs are scattered across dozens of EIPs, many still in draft. Nobody had tried to build all of them into one codebase to see if they compose. So I did.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 23769
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 24376,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 24376,
                    "startIndex": 24375,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 24375
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 25073,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 24729,
                    "startIndex": 24376,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "ETH2030 (eth2030.com, https://github.com/jiayaoqijia/eth2030) is the result - an experimental reference implementation targeting the draft EF Protocol L1  roadmap, a working document from Ethereum's core protocol researchers (Ansgar, Barnabe, Francesco, Justin) mapping eight upgrade phases from Glamsterdam (mid-2026) through the Giga-Gas era (2030+). ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 25073,
                    "startIndex": 24729,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Built with agentic coding - Claude Code (Opus 4.6), approximately 6 days, $5,750 in API costs, 2.77 billion tokens. It passes all 36,126 official Ethereum state tests, embeds go-ethereum v1.17.0 for mainnet connectivity, and covers everything from Block Access Lists to post-quantum cryptography to a full RISC-V CPU for zero-knowledge proofs.\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.9529412,
                              "green": 0.8862745,
                              "red": 0.8117647
