                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 28830,
                    "startIndex": 27991,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "^ Burry has been banging so loudly about the AI bubble/fraud, he’s almost desperate. Yeah, so he’s focused on, number one, he’s focusing on human knowledge and not compute, and the ability to think, and think through things, and then potentially, it’s potential that the models will have to get so fast that they can think through problem spaces, almost brute-force thinking, seeing what comes up. I’m not sure how they evaluate their own thinking to know whether it’s robust and you know any of the thinking that they’ll do is useful. But anyway, yeah, there’s, he’s extrapolating kind of the current way we use LLMs as just, Well, often common people like him might use LLM’s as some kind of knowledge base. And then in the second point up to the no one to pay for the singularity um no and you can oh god this may be true i don’t know.\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "bold": true
