            },
            {
              "endIndex": 32767,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 32767,
                    "startIndex": 32695,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "This matters enormously, because not all white-collar work is the same.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 32695
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 32768,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 32768,
                    "startIndex": 32767,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 32767
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 32999,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 32999,
                    "startIndex": 32768,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Some professions produce a fixed number of outputs. If you run an accounting firm, clients want one tax return. One set of financials. Make that work 10x cheaper and you don't get 10x more demand. Those jobs are genuinely at risk.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 32768
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 33000,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 33000,
                    "startIndex": 32999,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 32999
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 33331,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 33331,
                    "startIndex": 33000,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "But software? If you make software cheap to create, the demand is effectively unlimited. There's a massive backlog of software that doesn't exist because it wasn't worth building at 2024 labor costs. Games, internal tools, niche automations, apps nobody bothered to spec out. Drop the cost 10x and you might unlock 50x the demand.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 33000
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 33332,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 33332,
                    "startIndex": 33331,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 33331
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 33510,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 33510,
                    "startIndex": 33332,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "This is Jevons Paradox again — the observation that making a resource more efficient often *increases* total consumption rather than decreasing it. The report never mentions it.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 33332
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 33511,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
