                }
              },
              "startIndex": 49340
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 49351,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 49351,
                    "startIndex": 49350,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 49350
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 49632,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 49632,
                    "startIndex": 49351,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The failures of both Meta and xAI to maintain parity with the frontier labs, along with the fact that the Chinese open weights models continue to lag by months, means that recursive AI self-improvement, if it happens, will likely be by a model from Google, OpenAI and/or Anthropic\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 49351
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 49633,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 49633,
                    "startIndex": 49632,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 49632
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 49913,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 49913,
                    "startIndex": 49633,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "It is possible that xAI catches up, certainly Musk has stated that he thinks they can in a year. And Meta still has excellent people and lots of compute. But if you view the critical period, for better or worse, as this year, it is a bad time for a lab to sit this out right now.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 49633
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 49914,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 49914,
                    "startIndex": 49913,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 49913
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 50407,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 50407,
                    "startIndex": 49914,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "^ Probably wrong. Meta can’t build software, I don’t think, but I think unusual high-quality data is key, and I think there’s a fundamental dilemma of bringing all information to bear all the time. Beauty is in the eye of the beholder. A model has to limit its output to the artifact, which means making a decision about prioritising what to say, and that priority/relevance is judged by the user. It may also make connections that don’t land with the user, or that readers are not ready for.\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "bold": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 49914
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 50408,
              "paragraph": {
