                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 52705
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 52987,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 52987,
                    "startIndex": 52706,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "I cannot stress enough how absolutely cooked CS, Soft Eng, Comp Eng and basically any tech/IT major is. Literally no one in my cohort bothers to write their own code anymore. People just hand in labs that are fully vibecoded and pass with grades above 90% and the profs do NOTHING\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 52706
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 52988,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 52988,
                    "startIndex": 52987,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 52987
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 53268,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 53268,
                    "startIndex": 52988,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "I got a 93 in my data structures class by putting in actual effort and it literally meant nothing because the average at the end of the sem was quite literally 90. It's just really demotivating and I understand why people just choose to use AI at this point. My GPA means nothing\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 52988
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 53269,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 53269,
                    "startIndex": 53268,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 53268
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 53500,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 53500,
                    "startIndex": 53269,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "During our first assignement of the semester, a guy literally sent me a raw .sln file with nothing else for his part of the work and I asked him \"where are your classes\" and he said \"how do i get those\". We are in our 2nd year....\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 53269
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 53501,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 53501,
                    "startIndex": 53500,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 53500
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 53646,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 53646,
                    "startIndex": 53501,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "inb4 elon qrts my tweet on some \"AI is the future!, our young minds need to live with it! 🎯🚀\" and the replies are filled with bots glazing him\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 53501
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 53647,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 53647,
                    "startIndex": 53646,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 53646
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 53906,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 53906,
                    "startIndex": 53647,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "I think there needs to be a pivot in the field academically and if people wanna use AI sure but profs should interview students about their code to see if they understand what they wrote. A few of my profs did this here and there but should be normalized imo\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 53647
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 53907,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 53907,
                    "startIndex": 53906,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 53906
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 55116,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 55116,
                    "startIndex": 53907,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "^ Will every job go through this? Do the abstractions of OO still matter? What is software engineering really teaching? Why aren’t they testing people with pen and paper and throwing people out? What really made a great engineer? Knowing syntax was always a tiny factor. Knowing anything that is in base libraries was no direct use. So what was it? It is probably general IQ, creative problem solving, art of the possible and systems thinking. We need subject knowledge to be able to consider the art of the possible and what things to compose and coordinate to create a solution. At what point does the model also do that? Right now, they suffer severe cognitive tunnelling. Moreover, a solution presented by an AI that spans too many concepts that the end user is blind to and requires the user to have some significant involvement in enabling will be rejected by the AI-user. For example, AI presents a load of Python code, some C++ and installing and extending a VM hypervisor on a bunch of nodes, might feel uncomfortable as an idea, and be rejected. So the engineer must have enough subject matter experience to feel comfortable, even in a world where AI is also doing the higher level solution design.\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "bold": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 53907
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 55117,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
