                }
              },
              "startIndex": 61595
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 61699,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 61699,
                    "startIndex": 61596,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Some guy called Shananka who wrote every tweet in the most hyperbolic style, retweeted by Cathie Wood:\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 61596
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 61700,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 61700,
                    "startIndex": 61699,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 61699
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 61824,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 61824,
                    "startIndex": 61700,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "of the country it sits in. And he is sending 80% of it off-planet because Earth literally cannot power what he is building.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 61700
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 61825,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 61825,
                    "startIndex": 61824,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 61824
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 62376,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 62376,
                    "startIndex": 61825,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Follow the mechanism. Terafab seeds the chips. Starship launches Optimus robots and solar arrays at 100 million tons per year. The robots mine lunar and asteroid regolith for silicon, iron, and nickel. They 3D-print more robots. They fabricate more solar panels. They assemble more AI satellites. Each satellite runs hotter-burning D3 chips designed specifically for vacuum, where free radiative cooling eliminates the thermal constraints that strangle every terrestrial data center on the planet. The nodes replicate. The replication is exponential.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 61825
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 62377,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 62377,
                    "startIndex": 62376,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 62376
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 62453,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 62453,
                    "startIndex": 62377,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "This is a Dyson Swarm bootstrap hidden inside a semiconductor announcement.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 62377
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 62454,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 62454,
                    "startIndex": 62453,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 62453
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 63056,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 63056,
                    "startIndex": 62454,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The math is public. The Sun outputs 3.828 times 10 to the 26th watts. A 2022 paper in Physica Scripta calculated that 5.5 billion satellites at 290 kilograms each, robotically manufactured from Mars resources, capture enough solar energy to meet all of Earth’s power needs within 50 years. A 2025 paper in Solar Energy Materials calculated a partial swarm capturing 4% of solar output yields 15.6 yottawatts, roughly a billion times current human civilization’s total energy budget. Musk just announced the factory that builds the chips that go inside the satellites that replicate themselves forever.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "lineSpacing": 100,
