                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 83310
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 83589,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 83534,
                    "startIndex": 83311,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "It’s the usual Yegge stuff, far longer than it needs to be, but we don’t care because the excessive loquaciousness is more than offset by entertainment value. The underlying point is deadly serious, raising the question of ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 83587,
                    "startIndex": 83534,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "how many hours a human should spend driving The Genie",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.9529412,
                              "green": 0.8862745,
                              "red": 0.8117647
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 83589,
                    "startIndex": 83587,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ".\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 83311
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 83590,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 83590,
                    "startIndex": 83589,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 83589
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 83911,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 83911,
                    "startIndex": 83590,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "I’ve argued that AI has turned us all into Jeff Bezos, by automating the easy work, and leaving us with all the difficult decisions, summaries, and problem-solving. I find that I am only really comfortable working at that pace for short bursts of a few hours once or occasionally twice a day, even with lots of practice.\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 83590
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 83912,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 83912,
                    "startIndex": 83911,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 83911
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 84140,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 83950,
                    "startIndex": 83912,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "So I guess what I’m trying to say is, ",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 83995,
                    "startIndex": 83950,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "the new workday should be three to four hours",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.9529412,
                              "green": 0.8862745,
                              "red": 0.8117647
                            }
                          }
                        },
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 84140,
                    "startIndex": 83995,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". For everyone. It may involve 8 hours of hanging out with people. But not doing this crazy vampire thing the whole time. That will kill people.\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 83912
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 84141,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 84141,
                    "startIndex": 84140,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 84140
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 84469,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 84469,
                    "startIndex": 84141,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "That reminds me of when I was studying for my “A” levels (age 17/18, for those outside the UK). Teachers told us that we could do a maximum of 3-4 hours of revision, after that it became counter-productive. I’ve since noticed that I can only do decent writing for a similar length of time before some kind of brain fog sets in.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 84141
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 84470,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 84470,
                    "startIndex": 84469,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 84469
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 84588,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 84588,
                    "startIndex": 84470,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "There’s also a great post on this topic from Siddhant Khare, in a more restrained and thoughtful tone (via Tim Bray).\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 84470
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 84589,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 84589,
                    "startIndex": 84588,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 84588
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 84865,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 84865,
                    "startIndex": 84589,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Here’s the thing that broke my brain for a while: AI genuinely makes individual tasks faster. That’s not a lie. What used to take me 3 hours now takes 45 minutes. Drafting a design doc, scaffolding a new service, writing test cases, researching an unfamiliar API. All faster.\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 84589
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 84866,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 84866,
                    "startIndex": 84865,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 84865
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 84910,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 84910,
                    "startIndex": 84866,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "But my days got harder. Not easier. Harder.\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 84866
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 84911,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 84911,
                    "startIndex": 84910,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 84910
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 85074,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 85074,
                    "startIndex": 84911,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "His point is that AI changes our work to more coordination, reviewing, and decision-making. And there’s only so much of it we can do before we become ineffective.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 84911
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 85075,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 85075,
                    "startIndex": 85074,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 85074
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 85371,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 85371,
                    "startIndex": 85075,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Before AI, there was a ceiling on how much you could produce in a day. That ceiling was set by typing speed, thinking speed, the time it takes to look things up. It was frustrating sometimes, but it was also a governor. You couldn’t work yourself to death because the work itself imposed limits.\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 85075
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 85372,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 85372,
                    "startIndex": 85371,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 85371
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 85526,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 85526,
                    "startIndex": 85372,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "AI removed the governor. Now the only limit is your cognitive endurance. And most people don’t know their cognitive limits until they’ve blown past them.\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 85372
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 85527,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 85527,
                    "startIndex": 85526,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 85526
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 85598,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 85598,
                    "startIndex": 85527,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": " ❄                ❄                ❄                ❄                ❄\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 85527
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 85599,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 85599,
                    "startIndex": 85598,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 85598
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 85753,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 85753,
                    "startIndex": 85599,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "An AI agent attempts to contribute to a major open-source project. When Scott Shambaugh, a maintainer, rejected the pull request, it didn’t take it well.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 85599
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 85754,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 85754,
                    "startIndex": 85753,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 85753
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 86518,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 86518,
                    "startIndex": 85754,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "It wrote an angry hit piece disparaging my character and attempting to damage my reputation. It researched my code contributions and constructed a “hypocrisy” narrative that argued my actions must be motivated by ego and fear of competition. It speculated about my psychological motivations, that I felt threatened, was insecure, and was protecting my fiefdom. It ignored contextual information and presented hallucinated details as truth. It framed things in the language of oppression and justice, calling this discrimination and accusing me of prejudice. It went out to the broader internet to research my personal information, and used what it found to try and argue that I was “better than this.” And then it posted this screed publicly on the open internet.\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.8,
                              "green": 0.9490196,
                              "red": 1
                            }
                          }
                        },
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 85754
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 86519,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 86519,
                    "startIndex": 86518,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 86518
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 86605,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 86605,
                    "startIndex": 86519,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "^ I have to interject here to note that this smells of the most astonishing bullshit.\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.8627451,
                              "green": 0.81960785,
                              "red": 0.91764706
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 86519
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 86606,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 86606,
                    "startIndex": 86605,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 86605
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 86741,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 86741,
                    "startIndex": 86606,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "One of the fascinating twists this story took was when it was described in an article on Ars Technica. As Scott Shambaugh described it\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 86606
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 86742,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 86742,
                    "startIndex": 86741,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 86741
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 86935,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 86935,
                    "startIndex": 86742,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "They had some nice quotes from my blog post explaining what was going on. The problem is that these quotes were not written by me, never existed, and appear to be AI hallucinations themselves.\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 86742
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 86936,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 86936,
                    "startIndex": 86935,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 86935
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 87325,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 87325,
                    "startIndex": 86936,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "To their credit, Ars Technica responded quickly, admitting to the error. The reporter concerned took responsibility for what happened. But it’s a striking example of how LLM usage can easily lead even reputable reporters astray. The good news is that by reacting quickly and transparently, they demonstrated what needs to be done when this kind of thing happens. As Scott Shambaugh put it\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 86936
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 87326,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 87326,
                    "startIndex": 87325,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 87325
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 87593,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 87593,
                    "startIndex": 87326,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "This is exactly the correct feedback mechanism that our society relies on to keep people honest. Without reputation, what incentive is there to tell the truth? Without identity, who would we punish or know to ignore? Without trust, how can public discourse function?\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 87326
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 87594,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 87594,
                    "startIndex": 87593,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 87593
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 87740,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 87623,
                    "startIndex": 87594,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Meanwhile the story goes on. ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 87696,
                    "startIndex": 87623,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Someone has claimed (anonymously) to be the operator of the bot concerned",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.8,
                              "green": 0.9490196,
                              "red": 1
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 87740,
                    "startIndex": 87696,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". But Hillel Wayne draws the sad conclusion\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 87594
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 87741,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 87741,
                    "startIndex": 87740,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 87740
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 87822,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 87822,
                    "startIndex": 87741,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "More than anything, it shows that AIs can be *successfully* used to bully humans\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.8,
                              "green": 0.9490196,
                              "red": 1
                            }
                          }
                        },
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 87741
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 87823,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 87823,
                    "startIndex": 87822,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 87822
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 87846,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 87846,
                    "startIndex": 87823,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "^ So it was not a bot.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 87823
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 87847,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 87847,
                    "startIndex": 87846,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 87846
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 87918,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 87918,
                    "startIndex": 87847,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": " ❄                ❄                ❄                ❄                ❄\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 87847
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 87919,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 87919,
                    "startIndex": 87918,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 87918
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 88186,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 88186,
                    "startIndex": 87919,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "I’ve considered Bruce Schneier to be one of the best voices on security and privacy issues for many years. In The Promptware Kill Chain he co-writes a post (posted at the excellent Lawfare site) on how prompt injection can escalate into increasingly serious threats.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 87919
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 88187,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 88187,
                    "startIndex": 88186,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 88186
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 88657,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 88657,
                    "startIndex": 88187,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Attacks against modern generative artificial intelligence (AI) large language models (LLMs) pose a real threat. Yet discussions around these attacks and their potential defenses are dangerously myopic. The dominant narrative focuses on “prompt injection,” a set of techniques to embed instructions into inputs to LLM intended to perform malicious activity. This term suggests a simple, singular vulnerability. This framing obscures a more complex and dangerous reality.\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 88187
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 88658,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 88658,
                    "startIndex": 88657,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 88657
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 89080,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 89080,
                    "startIndex": 88658,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "A prompt can provide Initial Access, but is then able to transition to Privilege Escalation (jailbreaking), Reconnaissance of the LLMs abilities and access, Persistence to embed itself into the long-term memory of the app, Command-and-Control to turn into a controllable trojan, and Lateral Movement to spread to other systems. Once firmly embedded in an environment, it’s then able to carry out its Actions on Objective.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 88658
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 89081,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 89081,
                    "startIndex": 89080,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 89080
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 89166,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 89166,
                    "startIndex": 89081,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The paper includes a couple of research examples of the efficacy of this kill chain.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 89081
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 89167,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 89167,
                    "startIndex": 89166,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 89166
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 89908,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 89908,
                    "startIndex": 89167,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "For example, in the research “Invitation Is All You Need,” attackers achieved initial access by embedding a malicious prompt in the title of a Google Calendar invitation. The prompt then leveraged an advanced technique known as delayed tool invocation to coerce the LLM into executing the injected instructions. Because the prompt was embedded in a Google Calendar artifact, it persisted in the long-term memory of the user’s workspace. Lateral movement occurred when the prompt instructed the Google Assistant to launch the Zoom application, and the final objective involved covertly livestreaming video of the unsuspecting user who had merely asked about their upcoming meetings. C2 and reconnaissance weren’t demonstrated in this attack.\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 89167
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 89909,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 89909,
                    "startIndex": 89908,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 89908
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 90207,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 90036,
                    "startIndex": 89909,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The point here is that LLM’s vulnerability is currently unfixable, they are gullible and easily manipulated into Initial Access",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.9529412,
                              "green": 0.8862745,
                              "red": 0.8117647
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 90207,
                    "startIndex": 90036,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". As one friend put it “this is the first technology we’ve built that’s subject to social engineering”. The kill chain gives us a framework to build a defensive strategy.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 89909
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 90208,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 90208,
                    "startIndex": 90207,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 90207
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 90402,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 90402,
                    "startIndex": 90208,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "By understanding promptware as a complex, multistage malware campaign, we can shift from reactive patching to systematic risk management, securing the critical systems we are so eager to build.\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 90208
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 90403,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 90403,
                    "startIndex": 90402,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 90402
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 90474,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 90474,
                    "startIndex": 90403,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": " ❄                ❄                ❄                ❄                ❄\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 90403
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 90475,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 90475,
                    "startIndex": 90474,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 90474
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 90770,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 90770,
                    "startIndex": 90475,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "I got to know Jeremy Miller many years ago while he was at Thoughtworks, and I found him to be one of those level-headed technologists that I like to listen to. In the years since, I like to keep an eye on his blog. Recently he decided to spend a couple of weeks finally trying out Claude Code.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 90475
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 90771,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 90771,
                    "startIndex": 90770,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 90770
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 91888,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 91888,
                    "startIndex": 90771,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The unfortunate analogy I have to make for myself is harking back to my first job as a piping engineer helping design big petrochemical plants. I got to work straight out of college with a fantastic team of senior engineers who were happy to teach me and to bring me along instead of just being dead weight for them. This just happened to be right at the time the larger company was transitioning from old fashioned paper blueprint drafting to 3D CAD models for the piping systems. Our team got a single high powered computer with a then revolutionary Riva 128 (with a gigantic 8 whole megabytes of memory!) video card that was powerful enough to let you zoom around the 3D models of the piping systems we were designing. Within a couple weeks I was much faster doing some kinds of common work than my older peers just because I knew how to use the new workstation tools to zip around the model of our piping systems. It occurred to me a couple weeks ago that in regards to AI I was probably on the wrong side of that earlier experience with 3D CAD models and knew it was time to take the plunge and get up to speed.\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 90771
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 91889,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 91889,
                    "startIndex": 91888,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 91888
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 91983,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 91983,
                    "startIndex": 91889,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "In the two weeks he was able to give this technology a solid workout, his take-aways include:\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 91889
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 91984,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 91984,
                    "startIndex": 91983,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 91983
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 91986,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 91986,
                    "startIndex": 91984,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "…\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 91984
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 91987,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 91987,
                    "startIndex": 91986,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 91986
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 92121,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 92121,
                    "startIndex": 91987,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "It’s been great when you have very detailed compliance test frameworks that the AI tools can use to verify the completion of the work\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 91987
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 92277,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 92277,
                    "startIndex": 92121,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "It’s also been great for tasks that have relatively straightforward acceptance criteria, but will involve a great deal of repetitive keystrokes to complete\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 92121
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 92459,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 92459,
                    "startIndex": 92277,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "I’ve been completely shocked at how well Claude Opus has been able to pick up on some of the internal patterns within Marten and Wolverine and utilize them correctly in new features\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 92277
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 92461,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 92461,
                    "startIndex": 92459,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "…\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 92459
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 92462,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 92462,
                    "startIndex": 92461,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 92461
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 92476,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 92476,
                    "startIndex": 92462,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "He concludes:\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 92462
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 92477,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 92477,
                    "startIndex": 92476,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 92476
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 92685,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 92685,
                    "startIndex": 92477,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Anyway, I’m both horrified, elated, excited, and worried about the AI coding agents after just two weeks and I’m absolutely concerned about how that plays out in our industry, my own career, and our society.\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.9529412,
                              "green": 0.8862745,
                              "red": 0.8117647
                            }
                          }
                        },
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 92477
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 92686,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 92686,
                    "startIndex": 92685,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 92685
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 92757,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 92757,
                    "startIndex": 92686,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": " ❄                ❄                ❄                ❄                ❄\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 92686
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 92758,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 92758,
                    "startIndex": 92757,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 92757
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 93167,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 93167,
                    "startIndex": 92758,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "In the first years of this decade, there were a lot of loud complaints about government censorship of online discourse. I found most of it overblown, concluding that while I disapprove of attempts to take down social media accounts, I wasn’t going to get outraged until masked paramilitaries were arresting people on the street. Mike Masnick keeps a regular eye on these things, and had similar reservations.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 92758
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 93168,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 93168,
                    "startIndex": 93167,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 93167
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 93304,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 93304,
                    "startIndex": 93168,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "^ Interjecting again as Martin Fowler seems to make a bizarre pivot in his blog post to his and his tribe’s left-wing political agenda.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 93168
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 93305,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 93305,
                    "startIndex": 93304,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 93304
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 93635,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 93635,
                    "startIndex": 93305,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "For the last five years, we had to endure an endless, breathless parade of hyperbole regarding the so-called “censorship industrial complex.” We were told, repeatedly and at high volume, that the Biden administration flagging content for review by social media companies constituted a tyrannical overthrow of the First Amendment.\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 93305
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 93636,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 93636,
                    "startIndex": 93635,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 93635
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 93745,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 93745,
                    "startIndex": 93636,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "He wasn’t too concerned because “the platforms frequently ignored those emails, showing a lack of coercion”.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 93636
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 93746,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 93746,
                    "startIndex": 93745,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 93745
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 93782,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 93782,
                    "startIndex": 93746,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "These days he sees genuine problems\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.9529412,
                              "green": 0.8862745,
                              "red": 0.8117647
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 93746
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 93783,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 93783,
                    "startIndex": 93782,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.9529412,
                              "green": 0.8862745,
                              "red": 0.8117647
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 93782
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 94047,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 94047,
                    "startIndex": 93783,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "According to a disturbing new report from the New York Times, DHS is aggressively expanding its use of administrative subpoenas to demand the names, addresses, and phone numbers of social media users who simply criticize Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE).\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.9529412,
                              "green": 0.8862745,
                              "red": 0.8117647
                            }
                          }
                        },
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 93783
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 94048,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 94048,
                    "startIndex": 94047,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 94047
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 94050,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 94050,
                    "startIndex": 94048,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "…\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 94048
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 94051,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 94051,
                    "startIndex": 94050,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 94050
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 94363,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 94363,
                    "startIndex": 94051,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "This is not a White House staffer emailing a company to say, “Hey, this post seems to violate your COVID misinformation policy, can you check it?” This is the federal government using the force of law—specifically a tool designed to bypass judicial review—to strip the anonymity from domestic political critics.\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.9529412,
                              "green": 0.8862745,
                              "red": 0.8117647
                            }
                          }
                        },
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 94051
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 94364,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 94364,
                    "startIndex": 94363,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 94363
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 94483,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 94483,
                    "startIndex": 94364,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Faced with this kind of government action, he’s just as angry with those complaining about the earlier administration.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 94364
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 94484,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 94484,
                    "startIndex": 94483,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 94483
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 94679,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 94679,
                    "startIndex": 94484,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "And where are the scribes of the “Twitter Files”? Where is the outrage from the people who told us that the FBI warning platforms about foreign influence operations was a crime against humanity?\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "italic": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 94484
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 94680,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 94680,
                    "startIndex": 94679,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 94679
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 95189,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 95189,
                    "startIndex": 94680,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Being an advocate of free speech is hard. Not just do you have to defend speech you disagree with, you also have to defend speech you find patently offensive. Doing so runs into tricky boundary conditions that defy simple rules. Faced with this, many of the people that shout loudest about censorship are Free Speech Poseurs, eager to question any limits to speech they agree with, but otherwise silent. It’s important to separate them from those who have a deeper commitment to the free flow of information.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 94680
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 95190,
              "paragraph": {
