              },
              "startIndex": 96307
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 96357,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 96357,
                    "startIndex": 96308,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Michael Burry on Edison and electrification wave\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 96308
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 96358,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 96358,
                    "startIndex": 96357,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 96357
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 96437,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 96437,
                    "startIndex": 96358,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The trouble was not limited to hallowed names such as Westinghouse and Edison.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 96358
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 96655,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 96655,
                    "startIndex": 96437,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "From “Killing Complaints with Courtesy”: The Role of Relationship Building in the Success of the Early U.S. Central Power Stations (1890–1938) – a great read on the early electricity boom and how it all came together:\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 96437
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 97175,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 97175,
                    "startIndex": 96655,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "> “Within their first four decades of operation, countless new central stations across the United States went bankrupt or came close, while some private companies avoided bankruptcy by becoming municipally operated. The panics of 1893 and 1907 doomed many companies, including the Westinghouse Electric Company, which went bankrupt. A few years later, an Oklahoma newspaper claimed that many plants in the state had gone bankrupt, followed by many more companies whose mounting liabilities far exceeded company assets.”\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 96655
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 97178,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 97178,
                    "startIndex": 97175,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "> \n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 97175
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 97203,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 97203,
                    "startIndex": 97178,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "But wait, there is more.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 97178
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 97583,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 97583,
                    "startIndex": 97203,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "> “Rapid progress in technologies along the grid and quickly outdated equipment such as local transformers have led to precipitous depreciation of utility assets. This calculus was on the minds of Vinita Electric Light and Power Co. of Oklahoma when, in March 1910, it informed the public that although the company had not gone into bankruptcy, it had not made any money either.”\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 97203
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 97586,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 97586,
                    "startIndex": 97583,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "> \n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 97583
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 97755,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 97755,
                    "startIndex": 97586,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "This is not to say that electricity was not a great and glorious thing. From 1900 to 1910, electricity production increased 280% and generation capacity increased 375%.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 97586
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 97811,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 97811,
                    "startIndex": 97755,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Thomas Edison himself is heavily quoted in the article.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 97755
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 97995,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 97995,
                    "startIndex": 97811,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "> “Recently there has been sharp rivalry between the companies, and prices have been cut so that there has been little profit in the manufacture of electrical machinery for anybody...\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 97811
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 98370,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 98370,
                    "startIndex": 97995,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "> I think there are forty or fifty suits in which companies are interested. I do not suppose the consolidation will result in stopping the litigation. The papers in the cases are on file. In many cases there are principles involved which will govern in determining suits over patent rights with the Westinghouse Company. I suppose those suits will be carried to a decision.”\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 97995
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 98373,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 98373,
                    "startIndex": 98370,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "> \n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 98370
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 98423,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 98423,
                    "startIndex": 98373,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "More from Mr. Edison, in a bit of a bitter pique,\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 98373
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 98719,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 98719,
                    "startIndex": 98423,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "> “I cannot waste my time over electric lighting matters, for they are old. I ceased to worry over those things ten years ago, and I have a lot more new material on which to work. Electric lights are too old for me. I simply want to get as large dividends as possible from such stock as I hold.”\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 98423
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 98722,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 98722,
                    "startIndex": 98719,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "> \n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 98719
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 98890,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 98890,
                    "startIndex": 98722,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The decline of Edison Electric was partly due to Edison himself favoring direct current, while eventual competitors recognized alternating current was the way forward.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 98722
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 99050,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 99050,
                    "startIndex": 98890,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Those new alternating current competitors included General Electric and Westinghouse, both of which were brought to their knees in the financial panic of 1893.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 98890
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 99138,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 99138,
                    "startIndex": 99050,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Would you like me to summarize the key economic factors that led to these bankruptcies?\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 99050
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 99139,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 99139,
                    "startIndex": 99138,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 99138
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 99163,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 99163,
                    "startIndex": 99139,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "^ Compelling stuff.tbh.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 99139
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 99164,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 99164,
