              },
              "startIndex": 99163
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 99177,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 99177,
                    "startIndex": 99164,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "From Gemini \n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 99164
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 99178,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 99178,
                    "startIndex": 99177,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 99177
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 99436,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 99436,
                    "startIndex": 99178,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The parallel isn’t just a coincidence—it’s a historical pattern. Just as the 1892 merger created General Electric to stabilize a chaotic, debt-ridden industry, Big Tech is currently positioning itself as the \"stabilizer\" and \"consolidator\" of the AI sector.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 99178
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 99590,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 99590,
                    "startIndex": 99436,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The \"swooping in\" isn’t just a future possibility; it is already happening through a strategy often called \"Pseudo-Acquisitions\" or \"Reverse Acquihires.\"\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 99436
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 99629,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 99629,
                    "startIndex": 99590,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "1. The Playbook: \"Pseudo-Acquisitions\"\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 99590
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 99836,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 99836,
                    "startIndex": 99629,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "In the 1890s, Edison and Thomson-Houston merged to pool cash and talent while avoiding bankruptcy. Today, Big Tech uses creative deals to \"consume\" companies while avoiding the gaze of antitrust regulators:\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 99629
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 100104,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 100104,
                    "startIndex": 99836,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": " * Microsoft and Inflection AI: In 2024, Microsoft paid $650 million to license Inflection’s models and hired almost its entire 70-person staff, including the founders. Effectively, they \"consumed\" the company without a formal merger that could be blocked by the FTC.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 99836
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 100316,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 100316,
                    "startIndex": 100104,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": " * Google and Character.AI: Google struck a $2.7 billion deal to license the startup’s technology and hired its co-founders. The startup remains independent on paper, but its \"DNA\" has been absorbed into Google.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 100104
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 100477,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 100477,
                    "startIndex": 100316,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": " * Amazon and Adept: Amazon followed the same script, hiring the CEO and key researchers while paying a licensing fee for the startup’s \"agentic\" AI technology.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 100316
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 100529,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 100529,
                    "startIndex": 100477,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "2. The Infrastructure Trap (The \"Utility\" Parallel)\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 100477
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 100714,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 100714,
                    "startIndex": 100529,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "In the 1892 article, Edison noted that companies were going broke because building \"electric railways\" and \"central stations\" required massive capital that startups simply didn't have.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 100529
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 100934,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 100934,
                    "startIndex": 100714,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": " * Today's \"Power Plants\": The modern equivalent of a central station is the Data Center. Big Tech firms (Microsoft, Google, Meta, Amazon) are the only ones with the multi-billion dollar \"balance sheets\" to build these.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 100714
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 101192,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 101192,
                    "startIndex": 100934,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": " * Energy as the Bottleneck: Just as early electric companies fought over grid access, Big Tech is now securing nuclear and geothermal energy to power their AI. Startups like Anthropic or OpenAI are increasingly dependent on Big Tech's \"grid\" to even exist.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 100934
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 101249,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 101249,
                    "startIndex": 101192,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "3. The Shift from \"Innovation\" to \"Hardware & Dividends\"\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 101192
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 101441,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 101441,
                    "startIndex": 101249,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Edison’s 1892 quote—\"I cannot waste my time over electric lighting matters, for they are old... I simply want to get as large dividends as possible\"—is echoed in how the industry is maturing.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 101249
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 101597,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 101597,
                    "startIndex": 101441,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": " * The \"Commodity\" Phase: Large Language Models (LLMs) are becoming \"commodities,\" much like electricity was becoming \"ordinary hardware\" in Edison's time.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 101441
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 101840,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 101840,
                    "startIndex": 101597,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": " * Big Tech's Strategy: They are moving away from the excitement of \"new models\" toward integration. They don't want to just build the \"lightbulb\" (the AI); they want to own the \"utility company\" (the Cloud/GPU infrastructure) that powers it.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 101597
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 101869,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 101869,
                    "startIndex": 101840,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The Verdict: Will they fail?\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 101840
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 102129,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 102129,
                    "startIndex": 101869,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The \"model companies\" (OpenAI, Anthropic, Cohere) that don't find a clear path to profitability are likely to follow the fate of the \"Vinita Electric Light and Power Co.\" mentioned in your documents: they may not go bankrupt, but they won't make money either.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 101869
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 102289,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 102289,
                    "startIndex": 102129,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "When their venture capital runs dry, Big Tech is standing by with \"licensing deals\" that look like lifeboats but function as vacuum cleaners for talent and IP.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 102129
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 102427,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 102427,
                    "startIndex": 102289,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Would you like me to look into specific \"exit strategies\" being discussed for companies like Anthropic or Cohere in current 2026 reports?\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 102289
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 102428,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 102428,
                    "startIndex": 102427,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 102427
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 102438,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 102438,
                    "startIndex": 102428,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "ChatGPT -\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 102428
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 102439,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 102439,
                    "startIndex": 102438,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 102438
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 102619,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 102619,
                    "startIndex": 102439,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "You’re not wrong to see the pattern. Big infrastructure waves almost always start chaotic, overcapitalized, and idealistic… then end consolidated, capital-intensive, and ruthless.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 102439
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 102620,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 102620,
                    "startIndex": 102619,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 102619
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 102667,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 102667,
                    "startIndex": 102620,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Let’s ground this in reality instead of vibes.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 102620
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 102668,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
