              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 157477,
                    "startIndex": 157450,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Sand & The Next Bottleneck\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "headingId": "h.9jv4cjnxk0o0",
                  "namedStyleType": "HEADING_2"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 157450
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 157629,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 157629,
                    "startIndex": 157477,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "I asked Gemini Deep Research to look into sand but it was distracted by my alter aim to research ;the next bottleneck in AI’ and has come up with this.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 157477
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 157630,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 157630,
                    "startIndex": 157629,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 157629
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 157766,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 157766,
                    "startIndex": 157630,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The **friction slowing down Artificial Intelligence** — A simple look at the limits in infrastructure, energy, and people for 2026–2030\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 157630
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 157767,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 157767,
                    "startIndex": 157766,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 157766
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 158334,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 157847,
                    "startIndex": 157767,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "History shows that new technologies usually don't run out of basic raw materials",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.9529412,
                              "green": 0.8862745,
                              "red": 0.8117647
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 157849,
                    "startIndex": 157847,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 157972,
                    "startIndex": 157849,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Instead, they get held back by the energy, difficulty, and exact steps needed to turn those materials into something useful",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.9529412,
                              "green": 0.8862745,
                              "red": 0.8117647
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 158054,
                    "startIndex": 157972,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". For computer chips, silicon is everywhere in the Earth's crust (about 28%), but ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 158133,
                    "startIndex": 158054,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "the real limit is purifying it to an extremely high level — \"eleven nines\" pure",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.8,
                              "green": 0.8,
                              "red": 0.95686275
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 158334,
                    "startIndex": 158133,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". Beach sand is common, but the super-pure silica sand needed for solar panels and fiber optics makes up only a tiny part of what's mined, and it needs careful processing to become \"electronic-grade.\"\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 157767
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 158335,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 158335,
                    "startIndex": 158334,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 158334
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 158684,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 158684,
                    "startIndex": 158335,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Now, as AI grows fast in its second decade, the same kind of limit has appeared. The main thing holding back AI progress has shifted from ideas and software to real-world physical stuff: not enough electricity, hard-to-build chip packaging, running out of good training data, and too few skilled people to make these systems work in the real world.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 158335
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 158685,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 158685,
                    "startIndex": 158684,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 158684
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 158744,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 158744,
                    "startIndex": 158685,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "**The Electricity Wall and the Energy Connection Problem**\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 158685
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 158745,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 158745,
                    "startIndex": 158744,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 158744
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 159160,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 159160,
                    "startIndex": 158745,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "As more people and companies use AI, data centers are changing from big and spread out to super dense and power-hungry. In 2026, the key things for AI setups are having enough power, being in safe locations, and handling much higher electricity use per equipment rack. Training and running the biggest AI models now need gigawatts of power, which is pushing old data center designs and power grids to their limits.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 158745
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 159161,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 159161,
                    "startIndex": 159160,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 159160
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 159461,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 159461,
                    "startIndex": 159161,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "This \"Power Wall\" means AI software can keep improving in theory, but the physical setup can't keep up. Building an AI-ready data center now takes about 12–24 months, but upgrading the power grid, getting approvals for new power lines, and starting new power plants usually takes 5–10 years or more.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 159161
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 159462,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 159462,
                    "startIndex": 159461,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 159461
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 159915,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 159539,
                    "startIndex": 159462,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "This timing difference has changed plans for big tech companies and AI labs. ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 159611,
                    "startIndex": 159539,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The biggest limit for growing is now electricity availability, not chips",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.9529412,
                              "green": 0.8862745,
                              "red": 0.8117647
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 159915,
                    "startIndex": 159611,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". Many reports show companies have piles of AI hardware sitting unused because they can't get the power to run it. In the US, after years of little growth in power supply, there's almost no extra capacity left for new data centers. Every new gigawatt of need requires a new gigawatt of power generation.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 159462
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 159916,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 159916,
                    "startIndex": 159915,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 159915
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 159966,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 159966,
                    "startIndex": 159916,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "**Moving to On-Site Power and Grid Independence**\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 159916
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 159967,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 159967,
                    "startIndex": 159966,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 159966
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 160345,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 160345,
                    "startIndex": 159967,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "To avoid long waits for grid connections, top AI companies are using \"extreme\" power solutions. They're building their own power generation right at the data center site so they can run independently, at least for the first few years. Natural gas is the go-to choice for this bridge because it can be set up quickly and provide steady power — faster than renewables or nuclear.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 159967
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 160346,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 160346,
                    "startIndex": 160345,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 160345
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 160370,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 160370,
                    "startIndex": 160346,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Here are some examples:\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 160346
            },
            {
