              "endIndex": 168195,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 168195,
                    "startIndex": 168147,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "**Conclusion: From Digital to Physical Limits**\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 168147
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 168196,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 168196,
                    "startIndex": 168195,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 168195
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 168494,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 168494,
                    "startIndex": 168196,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "In 2026 and beyond, AI's main limit is a mix of physical, energy, and people issues. We've fixed some chip problems, but bigger slow-moving ones like power grids hold us back. The Power Wall is the hardest ceiling — without big grid changes, AI growth stays capped by real megawatts and equipment.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 168196
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 168495,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 168495,
                    "startIndex": 168494,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 168494
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 168789,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 168789,
                    "startIndex": 168495,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "By 2030, winners will be those ready at the base: planning power early, locking in packaging supply, and building AI engineer teams to make models work. Easy digital growth ends; now it's about mastering the physical side — from pure silicon to the power grid — to win in the intelligence era.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 168495
            },
