            },
            {
              "endIndex": 177829,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 177829,
                    "startIndex": 177828,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 177828
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 177890,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 177890,
                    "startIndex": 177829,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "It's Too Obvious. What If AI Doesn't Actually End The World?\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 177829
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 177891,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 177891,
                    "startIndex": 177890,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 177890
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 178171,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 178171,
                    "startIndex": 177891,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The stock market just erased -$800 BILLION in market cap because AI \"taking over the world\" is becoming the consensus view. That view is too obvious. And the \"obvious\" trade never actually wins. Before we begin, BOOKMARK this article and refer back to it over the next 12 months.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 177891
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 178172,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 178172,
                    "startIndex": 178171,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 178171
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 178487,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 178487,
                    "startIndex": 178172,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The doomsday scenario went viral because it captured something visceral. It framed AI not as a productivity tool, but as a macroeconomic destabilizer capable of triggering a negative feedback loop: layoffs lead to weaker consumption, weaker consumption leads to more automation, and automation accelerates layoffs.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 178172
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 178488,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 178488,
                    "startIndex": 178487,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 178487
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 178751,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 178751,
                    "startIndex": 178488,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "What's obviously true: AI is not another software feature or efficiency gain. It is a general-purpose capability shock that touches every white-collar workflow simultaneously. Unlikely any revolution in history, AI is getting better at EVERYTHING simultaneously.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 178488
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 178752,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 178752,
                    "startIndex": 178751,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 178751
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 178932,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 178932,
                    "startIndex": 178752,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "But, what if the doomsday scenario is false? It assumes demand is fixed, that productivity gains don’t expand markets, and that the system cannot adapt faster than the disruption.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 178752
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 178933,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 178933,
                    "startIndex": 178932,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 178932
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 179159,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 179159,
                    "startIndex": 178933,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "We believe there is a second path that is being dramatically underpriced. The same Anthropic “takedowns” that look like early signs of systemic collapse may ultimately be the start of the largest productivity expansion EVER. \n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 178933
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 179160,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 179160,
                    "startIndex": 179159,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 179159
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 179320,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 179320,
                    "startIndex": 179160,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "While the below analysis is not a certain outcome, it is important to remember that humanity has ALWAYS prevailed; and the free market ALWAYS works itself out.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 179160
            },
            {
