              "startIndex": 199046
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 199358,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 199356,
                    "startIndex": 199047,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Misunderstanding Inelastic Goods: Kobeissi argues AI will act as a massive \"invisible tax cut\" driving down living costs. As you correctly pointed out, housing, food, and energy do not magically become cheaper because an LLM can code. They are constrained by zoning laws, thermodynamics, and physical scarcity",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.9529412,
                              "green": 0.8862745,
                              "red": 0.8117647
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 199358,
                    "startIndex": 199356,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ".\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 199047
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 199359,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 199359,
                    "startIndex": 199358,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 199358
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 199669,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 199394,
                    "startIndex": 199359,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The \"Abundance Ends Wars\" Fallacy: ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 199667,
                    "startIndex": 199394,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "This is historically illiterate, and you were right to call it nonsense. The Industrial Revolution created unprecedented abundance but directly fueled the imperial scramble for Africa and WW1 to secure the raw materials (molecules) required for that new production capacity",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.8,
                              "green": 0.8,
                              "red": 0.95686275
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
