                    "startIndex": 199670,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Glossing Over the Transition Period: Kobeissi dismisses the short-term disruption as mere \"margin compression.\" In financial markets, a rapid 5-year transition that destroys the collateral value of the SaaS and commercial real estate sectors is called a Depression. Keynes’ \"in the long run we are all dead\" applies here.\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.8,
                              "green": 0.8,
                              "red": 0.95686275
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 199670
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 199993,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 199993,
                    "startIndex": 199992,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 199992
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 200011,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 200011,
                    "startIndex": 199993,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "On Your Comments:\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 199993
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 200012,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 200012,
                    "startIndex": 200011,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 200011
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 200290,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 200290,
                    "startIndex": 200012,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The \"Puff Piece\" Assessment: You correctly identify this as a market cheerleader piece. Kobeissi conflates the long-term macro equilibrium (which is likely positive) with the short-term structural violence (which will ruin specific asset classes and heavily leveraged cohorts).\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 200012
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 200291,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 200291,
                    "startIndex": 200290,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 200290
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 200611,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 200431,
                    "startIndex": 200291,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Defensible Moats Post-AI: You ask what the real moats are if software and intelligence are commoditized. You correctly identify regulation. ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 200609,
                    "startIndex": 200431,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The ultimate post-AI moats will be: 1) Regulatory capture, 2) Hard physical assets (energy generation, land), 3) Proprietary data generation networks, and 4) Trusted human brands",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.9529412,
                              "green": 0.8862745,
                              "red": 0.8117647
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 200611,
                    "startIndex": 200609,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ".\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 200291
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 200612,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 200612,
                    "startIndex": 200611,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 200611
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 200922,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 200922,
                    "startIndex": 200612,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Offshore Precedents: You note that cheap white-collar labor (e.g., in India) has existed for decades without collapsing Western economies. However, human offshoring still has coordination friction, time-zone lags, and quality limits. Agentic AI removes the friction entirely, changing the scale of the threat.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 200612
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 200923,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 200923,
                    "startIndex": 200922,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 200922
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 200925,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 200925,
                    "startIndex": 200923,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "-\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 200923
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 200926,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 200926,
                    "startIndex": 200925,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 200925
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 200972,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 200972,
                    "startIndex": 200926,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Gemini 3.1 Pro Thinking on space data centers\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 200926
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 200973,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 200973,
                    "startIndex": 200972,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 200972
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 201996,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 201782,
                    "startIndex": 200973,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "While deploying solar-powered AI data centers in orbit via Starship seems to solve the terrestrial energy deficit, it immediately collides with the brutal thermodynamic realities of space. Space is cold, but it is also a vacuum, meaning it acts as a perfect insulator where convection cooling does not exist. A one-gigawatt AI training cluster generates one gigawatt of waste heat, which in space can only be dissipated through thermal radiation, requiring impossibly massive, material-heavy radiator arrays. Furthermore, the build-out is bottlenecked by the need to launch thousands of tons of Earth-bound resources—ultra-pure quartz, copper, and silicon—alongside heavy physical shielding required to protect highly sensitive, non-radiation-hardened GPUs from cosmic rays that cause catastrophic bit-flips. ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 201994,
                    "startIndex": 201782,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "When you add the physical bandwidth limits of transmitting exabytes of training data between Earth and orbit via RF or optical links, the logistical mass and complexity of an orbital data center become staggering",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.9529412,
                              "green": 0.8862745,
                              "red": 0.8117647
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 201996,
                    "startIndex": 201994,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ".\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 200973
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 201997,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 201997,
                    "startIndex": 201996,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 201996
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 202942,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 202133,
                    "startIndex": 201997,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Consequently, this orbital scenario absolutely acts as a strict brake on the accelerated 2026–2028 doomsday timeline proposed by Citrini",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.827451,
                              "green": 0.91764706,
                              "red": 0.8509804
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 202135,
                    "startIndex": 202133,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 202263,
                    "startIndex": 202135,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The dystopian \"human displacement spiral\" relies on compute scaling frictionlessly and exponentially in the immediate short term",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.9529412,
                              "green": 0.8862745,
                              "red": 0.8117647
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 202513,
                    "startIndex": 202263,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". However, engineering novel orbital thermal management systems, establishing autonomous space-construction robotics, and executing thousands of heavy-lift launches is a multi-decade megaproject, not a rapid workaround for tomorrow's grid shortages. ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 202700,
                    "startIndex": 202513,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Space infrastructure guarantees that the transition to artificial superintelligence remains tethered to the agonizingly slow, linear realities of heavy manufacturing and materials science",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.9529412,
                              "green": 0.8862745,
                              "red": 0.8117647
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 202942,
                    "startIndex": 202700,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". Ultimately, the laws of physics and supply chain logistics—whether applied on Earth or in Low Earth Orbit—ensure that the economic disruption will unfold over a prolonged, manageable horizon rather than a sudden, apocalyptic tipping point.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 201997
            },
