                  {
                    "endIndex": 208320,
                    "startIndex": 208319,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 208319
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 208567,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 208567,
                    "startIndex": 208320,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The Death of Bounded Rationality in Commerce: You will never overpay or forget to cancel a subscription again. Your personal agent will continuously optimize your overhead, destroying the profit margins of any company relying on consumer inertia.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 208320
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 208568,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 208568,
                    "startIndex": 208567,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 208567
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 208605,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 208605,
                    "startIndex": 208568,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Gemini 3.1 Pro Thinking final words:\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 208568
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 208606,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 208606,
                    "startIndex": 208605,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 208605
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 209684,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 208767,
                    "startIndex": 208606,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "I predict with 80% confidence that we will not experience catastrophic, macroeconomic mass layoffs (e.g., a sudden spike to 10–20% systemic unemployment) by 2028",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.827451,
                              "green": 0.91764706,
                              "red": 0.8509804
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 208769,
                    "startIndex": 208767,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ", ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 208937,
                    "startIndex": 208769,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "though we will undoubtedly see acute, localized bloodbaths in specific white-collar sectors like junior software development, copywriting, and bloated middle management",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.8,
                              "green": 0.8,
                              "red": 0.95686275
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 208939,
                    "startIndex": 208937,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 209256,
                    "startIndex": 208939,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The dystopian timeline fundamentally underestimates the friction of the physical world: energy grid deficits, data center supply chain bottlenecks, and the agonizingly slow pace of legacy corporate integration will stagger AI's rollout over a decade rather than a few quarters, acting as a natural macroeconomic brake",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.9529412,
                              "green": 0.8862745,
                              "red": 0.8117647
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 209258,
                    "startIndex": 209256,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 209682,
                    "startIndex": 209258,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Furthermore, as you correctly intuited, the Jevons paradox will take effect; as the cost of cognitive execution plummets, human ambition will scale proportionately, sparking an unprecedented boom in AI-wielding solo-entrepreneurs, hyper-automated micro-businesses, and new \"agent orchestration\" roles that will absorb displaced labor and create entirely new vectors of economic demand faster than the doomsday models predict",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.827451,
                              "green": 0.91764706,
                              "red": 0.8509804
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 209684,
                    "startIndex": 209682,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ".\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 208606
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 209685,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 209685,
                    "startIndex": 209684,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 209684
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 210034,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 209866,
                    "startIndex": 209685,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Your theory is absolutely correct and is the exact reason John Maynard Keynes’s famous 1930 prediction of a \"15-hour workweek\" completely failed. Economically, this is explained by ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 210032,
                    "startIndex": 209866,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Parkinson's Law (work expands to fill the time allotted for it), but anthropologically, work is our primary mechanism for establishing status, community, and identity",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.827451,
                              "green": 0.91764706,
                              "red": 0.8509804
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 210034,
                    "startIndex": 210032,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ".\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 209685
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 210035,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 210035,
                    "startIndex": 210034,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 210034
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 210511,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 210335,
                    "startIndex": 210035,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Even if AI automates all pure \"utility\" and \"survival\" tasks, humans will simply invent new, highly complex social games and subjective economies—much like the modern creator economy, high-end hospitality, or hyper-niche consulting—just to have a reason to interact, compete, and validate one another",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.827451,
                              "green": 0.91764706,
                              "red": 0.8509804
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 210511,
                    "startIndex": 210335,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". We don't just work to produce goods; we work to produce society. AI can execute the tasks, but it cannot replace the human psychological need for a socially recognized role.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 210035
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 210512,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 210512,
                    "startIndex": 210511,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 210511
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 210540,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 210540,
                    "startIndex": 210512,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Claude Opus 4.6 Conclusion:\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 210512
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 210541,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 210541,
                    "startIndex": 210540,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 210540
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 211447,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 210836,
                    "startIndex": 210541,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Where I'd push back on the overall framing: both the doom and abundance camps underweight the messiness of the middle path. The physical bottlenecks Gemini identifies (power walls, quartz supply chains, packaging constraints) are real brakes that make the 2028 crisis timeline implausibly fast, ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 210938,
                    "startIndex": 210836,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "but they don't prevent a grinding, sector-by-sector repricing that's painful without being apocalyptic",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.8,
                              "green": 0.9490196,
                              "red": 1
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 211447,
                    "startIndex": 210938,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". Your own prediction at the end — localized bloodbaths but not systemic collapse, with Jevons paradox eventually generating new demand — strikes me as the most defensible position, though I'd note it still leaves open the nasty distributional question: the transition may be \"manageable\" in aggregate GDP terms while being devastating for specific demographic cohorts (mid-career white-collar professionals with mortgages) who lack the time or temperament to reinvent themselves as AI-wielding solopreneurs.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 210541
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 211448,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 211448,
                    "startIndex": 211447,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 211447
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 211450,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 211450,
                    "startIndex": 211448,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "-\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 211448
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 211451,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 211451,
                    "startIndex": 211450,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 211450
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 211461,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 211461,
                    "startIndex": 211451,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Sam Korus\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 211451
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 211472,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 211472,
                    "startIndex": 211461,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "@skorusARK\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 211461
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 211473,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 211473,
                    "startIndex": 211472,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 211472
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 211694,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 211694,
                    "startIndex": 211473,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The harsh truth is that there is tons of white collar bloat in companies now. The economy probably hit harder if that bloat is removed, because there isn't a magical tool creating a boom of productivity and new products.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 211473
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 211695,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 211695,
                    "startIndex": 211694,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 211694
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 211829,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 211829,
                    "startIndex": 211695,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Having AI boost productivity and create new businesses is good for the economy. There will be job displacements and new job creation.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 211695
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 211830,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 211830,
                    "startIndex": 211829,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 211829
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 211942,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 211942,
                    "startIndex": 211830,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "^ This is true, and widespread, and profoundly contradictory for the thesis of decimation in white collar work.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 211830
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 211943,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 211943,
                    "startIndex": 211942,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 211942
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 211945,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 211945,
                    "startIndex": 211943,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "-\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 211943
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 211946,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 211946,
                    "startIndex": 211945,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 211945
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 211993,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 211993,
                    "startIndex": 211946,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "> To get it out of my system, I blog about it:\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 211946
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 211994,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 211994,
                    "startIndex": 211993,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 211993
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 212086,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 212086,
                    "startIndex": 211994,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The Myth of the Perfectly Efficient Firm: Why AI Won't Trigger an Immediate Jobs Apocalypse\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 211994
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 212087,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 212087,
                    "startIndex": 212086,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 212086
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 212954,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 212382,
                    "startIndex": 212087,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "AI will initially increase bloat. Paradoxically, because corporate managers love empire-building, their first instinct won't be to fire their team; it will be to demand budget for \"Enterprise AI Tools\" and hire a new layer of \"AI Prompt Managers\" and \"AI Compliance Officers\" to oversee the bots",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.827451,
                              "green": 0.91764706,
                              "red": 0.8509804
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 212954,
                    "startIndex": 212382,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". In the realities of corporate game theory, a manager's salary, bonus, and social prestige are directly correlated to their headcount and budget. This classic principal-agent problem means that while shareholders crave lean profitability, the middle managers and executives controlling the daily operations optimize for status and job security. Rather than ruthlessly streamlining operations, their rational, self-interested move is to use AI as a justification to expand their domain, layering new technical bureaucracy directly over the old administrative bureaucracy.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 212087
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 212955,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 212955,
                    "startIndex": 212954,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 212954
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 213919,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 213919,
                    "startIndex": 212955,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "This behavioral reality exposes a fatal flaw in recent dystopian financial models, such as Citrini7’s viral \"2028 Global Intelligence Crisis\" thought exercise. That thesis posits a frictionless, devastating displacement spiral where incumbents rapidly fire white-collar workers and funnel the savings into compute, triggering a macroeconomic collapse. But this doomsday scenario assumes corporations are perfectly rational efficiency maximizers. They absolutely are not. If large firms were perfect efficiency engines, JPMorgan Chase wouldn't need 63,000 software engineers to maintain its infrastructure while a team of just seven people built and scaled Instagram to millions of users long before the era of generative AI. The Citrini7 model underestimates the sheer weight of technical debt and institutional inertia, failing to recognize that legacy corporate structures possess a biological immune response that actively resists sudden, localized efficiency.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 212955
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 213920,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 213920,
                    "startIndex": 213919,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 213919
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 214897,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 214897,
                    "startIndex": 213920,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The underlying truth is that humans instinctively conspire to make work for each other. Work is fundamentally a social activity driven by companionship, status games, and the psychological comfort of safety in numbers. Diffusion of responsibility is a powerful force; if a project fails in a bloated team of fifty, the blame easily dissipates, but if it fails in a highly automated team of three, you are fired. Therefore, hiring remains the ultimate corporate risk-mitigation strategy. Furthermore, Parkinson’s Law dictates that as you add people, the internal communication friction grows exponentially, necessitating even more people just to support the expanded team. Very few salaried employees will voluntarily deploy AI to automate themselves out of a job because the corporate incentive structure actively punishes it. If you automate your daily tasks, the firm captures 100% of the financial upside, and you are rewarded with either a doubled workload or a pink slip.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 213920
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 214898,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 214898,
                    "startIndex": 214897,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 214897
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 215797,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 215797,
                    "startIndex": 214898,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Ultimately, this deeply ingrained human friction will act as a massive macroeconomic shock absorber against sudden, algorithmic mass layoffs. As anthropologist David Graeber noted, a vast amount of modern corporate work exists purely for regulatory compliance, institutional signaling, or corporate ego—the so-called \"bullshit jobs\" of the white-collar world. AI is remarkably good at executing raw cognitive tasks, but it is entirely incapable of playing corporate politics, attending trust-building golf retreats, or serving as a human scapegoat for a vice president's bad decision. Because the corporate ecosystem optimizes for social hierarchies, empire-building, and a quiet life just as fiercely as it optimizes for profit, the AI transition inside large enterprises won't be an overnight, apocalyptic purge. It will be a slow, highly politicized, and surprisingly bloated bureaucratic crawl.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 214898
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 215798,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 215798,
                    "startIndex": 215797,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 215797
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 215800,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
