                }
              },
              "startIndex": 225646
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 225943,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 225943,
                    "startIndex": 225647,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Despite the macroeconomic community struggling to forecast 2-month-forward payroll growth with any reliable accuracy, the forward path of labor destruction can apparently be inferred with significant certainty from a hypothetical scenario posted on Substack: The 2028 Global Intelligence Crisis.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 225647
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 225944,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 225944,
                    "startIndex": 225943,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 225943
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 226280,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 226280,
                    "startIndex": 225944,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "We wrote last week that we see the near-term dynamics around the AI capex story as inflationary, but given markets are focused on the forward narrative, we outline a more constructive take on the end state below. Before that, however, it’s worth reflecting that the imminent disintermediation narrative rests on the speed of diffusion.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 225944
            },
