              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 227688,
                    "startIndex": 227646,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Recursive Technology ≠ Recursive Adoption\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 227646
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 227689,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 227689,
                    "startIndex": 227688,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 227688
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 228367,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 227859,
                    "startIndex": 227689,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The current debate around artificial intelligence conflates the recursive potential of the technology with expectations of recursive economic deployment. In other words, ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 228058,
                    "startIndex": 227859,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "because AI systems can improve themselves or accelerate their own capabilities, commentators are extrapolating a future in which automation and productivity compound indefinitely at exponential rates",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.827451,
                              "green": 0.91764706,
                              "red": 0.8509804
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 228237,
                    "startIndex": 228058,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". Technological diffusion has historically followed an S-curve. Early adoption is slow and expensive. Growth accelerates as costs fall, and complementary infrastructure develops. ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 228365,
                    "startIndex": 228237,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Eventually, saturation sets in, and the marginal adopter is less productive or less profitable which causes growth to decelerate",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.827451,
                              "green": 0.91764706,
                              "red": 0.8509804
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 228367,
                    "startIndex": 228365,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ".\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 227689
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 228368,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 228368,
                    "startIndex": 228367,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 228367
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 228676,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 228676,
                    "startIndex": 228368,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Despite this – markets often extrapolate the acceleration phase linearly but history implies pace of adoption plateaus as organizational integration is costly, regulation emerges and diminishing marginal returns exist in economic deployment. The risk of displacement declines with a slower pace of adoption.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 228368
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 228677,
