                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 228872
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 229089,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 229089,
                    "startIndex": 228873,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Source: Citadel Securities, BLS, St Louis Fed, Real Time Population Survey International Telecommunication Union. Figures are for illustrative purposes only. Past performance figures do not guarantee future results.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 228873
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 229090,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 229090,
                    "startIndex": 229089,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 229089
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 229934,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 229226,
                    "startIndex": 229090,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Furthermore, it is well acknowledged that training and inference requires significant semiconductor capacity, data centers, and energy. ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 229346,
                    "startIndex": 229226,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Displacing white collar work would require orders of magnitude more compute intensity than the current level utilization",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.827451,
                              "green": 0.91764706,
                              "red": 0.8509804
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 229934,
                    "startIndex": 229346,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". If automation expands rapidly, demand for compute definitionally rises, pushing up its marginal cost. If the marginal cost of compute rises above the marginal cost of human labor for certain tasks, substitution will not occur, creating a natural economic boundary. This dynamic contrasts sharply with narratives assuming frictionless replication of intelligence. Even if algorithms improve recursively, economic deployment remains bounded by physical capital, energy availability, regulatory approvals, and organizational change. Recursive capability does not imply recursive adoption.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 229090
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 229935,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 229935,
                    "startIndex": 229934,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 229934
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 229973,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 229973,
                    "startIndex": 229935,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Productivity Shocks Are Supply Shocks\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 229935
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 229974,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 229974,
                    "startIndex": 229973,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 229973
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 231348,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 229987,
                    "startIndex": 229974,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "At its core, ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 230157,
                    "startIndex": 229987,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "AI-driven automation is a productivity shock. Productivity shocks are positive supply shocks: they lower marginal costs, expand potential output, and increase real income",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.827451,
                              "green": 0.91764706,
                              "red": 0.8509804
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 230387,
                    "startIndex": 230157,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". They are in isolation disinflationary and growth-enhancing in the medium term. Historically, every major technological advance: steam power, electrification, the internal combustion engine, computing, has followed this pattern. ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 230512,
                    "startIndex": 230387,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The counterargument suggests that AI differs because it displaces labor income directly, thereby suppressing aggregate demand",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.9529412,
                              "green": 0.8862745,
                              "red": 0.8117647
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 230592,
                    "startIndex": 230512,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". If firms produce more at lower cost, prices fall or margins expand (or both). ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 230674,
                    "startIndex": 230592,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Lower prices increase real purchasing power, which generally increases consumption",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.827451,
                              "green": 0.91764706,
                              "red": 0.8509804
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 230676,
                    "startIndex": 230674,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 230741,
                    "startIndex": 230676,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Higher margins increase retained earnings and investment capacity",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.827451,
                              "green": 0.91764706,
                              "red": 0.8509804
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 231095,
                    "startIndex": 230741,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". If output rises and real GDP increases then by national income accounting identity something must be rising on the demand side: Consumption, investment, government spending, or net exports must be increasing (more here). A scenario in which productivity surges but aggregate demand collapses while measured output rises violates accounting identities. ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 231267,
                    "startIndex": 231095,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "For AI to generate a sustained macro contraction one must assume that labor income falls and no compensating rise occurs in investment, fiscal transfers, or external demand",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.9529412,
                              "green": 0.8862745,
                              "red": 0.8117647
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 231348,
                    "startIndex": 231267,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". The surge in new business formation is an interesting point of reference here.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 229974
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 231349,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 231349,
                    "startIndex": 231348,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 231348
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 231393,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 231393,
                    "startIndex": 231349,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "New Business Formation is Rapidly Expanding\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 231349
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 231437,
