                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Source: Citadel Securities, US Census Bureau. Figures are for illustrative purposes only. Past performance figures do not guarantee future results\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 231441
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 231589,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 231589,
                    "startIndex": 231588,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 231588
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 231624,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 231624,
                    "startIndex": 231589,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Substitution Elasticity Constraint\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 231589
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 231625,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 231625,
                    "startIndex": 231624,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 231624
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 232862,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 231673,
                    "startIndex": 231625,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The critical variable in AI displacement is the ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 231912,
                    "startIndex": 231673,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "elasticity of substitution between AI capital and labor. If that elasticity is extremely high – i.e. firms can substitute nearly all human labor with automated systems at relatively stable cost – then labor’s share of income could collapse",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.8,
                              "green": 0.9490196,
                              "red": 1
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 232009,
                    "startIndex": 231912,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". In such a world, capital income rises dramatically while wage income contracts. But even here, ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 232177,
                    "startIndex": 232009,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "aggregate demand does not automatically implode. Capital income has a lower marginal propensity to consume than wage income, but it does not have zero spending velocity",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.9529412,
                              "green": 0.8862745,
                              "red": 0.8117647
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 232394,
                    "startIndex": 232177,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". Profits can be reinvested, distributed, taxed, or spent. For demand to fall structurally, redistribution mechanisms would need to fail persistently, and investment opportunities would need to dry up simultaneously. ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 232560,
                    "startIndex": 232394,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Democratic nations facing such displacement risk would generally be expected to err towards in regulatory and fiscal policy shifts that offset the worst-case outcomes",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.827451,
                              "green": 0.91764706,
                              "red": 0.8509804
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 232862,
                    "startIndex": 232560,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ", further limiting substitution elasticity. Moreover – there is little evidence of AI disruption in labor market data as of today. In fact, the forward-looking components of our labor market tracking have improved and AI data center construction appears to be driving a pick-up in construction hiring.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 231625
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 232863,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 232863,
                    "startIndex": 232862,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 232862
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 232922,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 232922,
                    "startIndex": 232863,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "US Labor Market Tracking Continues To Point to Improvement\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
