                }
              },
              "startIndex": 233032
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 233035,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 233035,
                    "startIndex": 233034,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 233034
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 233202,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 233202,
                    "startIndex": 233035,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Source: Citadel Securities, Bloomberg, BLS, ADP, Revelio, Indeed. Figures are for illustrative purposes only. Past performance figures do not guarantee future results\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 233035
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 233203,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 233203,
                    "startIndex": 233202,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 233202
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 234059,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 233432,
                    "startIndex": 233203,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The economy contains a vast array of tasks: physical, relational, regulatory, supervisory – that are costly to automate. Even cognitive automation faces coordination frictions, liability constraints, and trust barriers. It seems ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 233521,
                    "startIndex": 233432,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "more likely that AI will be a complement rather than a substitute for labor in many areas",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.827451,
                              "green": 0.91764706,
                              "red": 0.8509804
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 233537,
                    "startIndex": 233521,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". Historically, ",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 233633,
                    "startIndex": 233537,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "technological revolutions have altered task composition rather than eliminated labor as an input",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.9529412,
                              "green": 0.8862745,
                              "red": 0.8117647
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 234059,
                    "startIndex": 233633,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ". To produce a negative demand shock large enough to overwhelm output expansion, one must assume near-total automation of economically relevant labor combined with extremely weak redistributive responses. To frame this debate correctly one can simply ask, was the advent of Microsoft office a complement or substitute for office workers? Ex-ante the concern skewed towards substitution, ex post it appears a clear complement.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 233203
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 234060,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 234060,
                    "startIndex": 234059,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 234059
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 234117,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 234117,
                    "startIndex": 234060,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Data Centre Construction is Boosting Construction Hiring\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
