            {
              "endIndex": 92,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 92,
                    "startIndex": 1,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Dwarkesh Patel, Silicon Valley latest podcast darling, saying something deeply unpopular. \n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 1
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 160,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 160,
                    "startIndex": 92,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "operation, or transportation of computers, robots, data, or energy.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 92
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 161,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 161,
                    "startIndex": 160,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 160
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 373,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 373,
                    "startIndex": 161,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Also, international catch-up growth may end. Poor countries historically grew faster by combining their cheap labor with imported capital/know-how. Without labor as a bottleneck, their main value-add disappears.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 161
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 374,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 374,
                    "startIndex": 373,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 373
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 1009,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 1009,
                    "startIndex": 374,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Inequality seems especially hard to justify in this world. So if we don’t want inequality to just keep increasing forever - with the descendants of the most patient and sophisticated of today’s AI investors controlling all the galaxies - what can we do? The obvious place to start is with Piketty’s headline recommendation: highly and progressively tax wealth. This might discourage saving, but it would no longer penalize those who have earned a lot by their hard work and creativity. The wealth - even the investment decisions - will be made by the robots, and they will work just as hard and smart however much we tax their owners.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 374
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 1010,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 1010,
                    "startIndex": 1009,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 1009
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 1402,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 1402,
                    "startIndex": 1010,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "But taxing capital is pointless if people can just shift their future investment to lower tax countries. And since capital stocks could grow really fast (robots building robots and all that), pretty soon tax havens go from marginal outposts to the majority of global GDP. But how do you get global coordination on taxing capital, when the benefits to defecting are so high and so accessible?\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 1010
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 1403,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 1403,
                    "startIndex": 1402,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 1402
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 1597,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 1597,
                    "startIndex": 1403,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Full automation will probably lead to ever-increasing inequality. We don’t see an obvious solution to this problem. And we think it’s weird how little thought has gone into what to do about it.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 1403
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 1598,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 1598,
                    "startIndex": 1597,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 1597
            },
