                          "weight": 400
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 11789,
                    "startIndex": 11582,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": " By restoring Venezuelan production (which has dropped from 3.5 million to roughly 1 million barrels per day), the U.S. hopes to increase global supply and drive down gasoline prices for American consumers.\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "foregroundColor": {
                          "color": {
