                          "weight": 400
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 15304,
                    "startIndex": 15018,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": " Without the \"bridge\" role, the UK is often treated by the current U.S. administration as just another mid-sized power. This \"downgrading\" is what fuels the skepticism you hear on podcasts—a feeling that the UK is being ignored by its \"child\" while being locked out by its \"neighbors.\"\n",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "foregroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.12156863,
                              "green": 0.12156863,
                              "red": 0.12156863
