              "startIndex": 18073
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 18113,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 18113,
                    "startIndex": 18074,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "London School Economics prof. Garicano\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 18074
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 18114,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 18114,
                    "startIndex": 18113,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 18113
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 18747,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 18263,
                    "startIndex": 18114,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "In the past, many used to say \"the US is saying it is democracy but it is oil\". This time, it is the opposite. Trump says it is oil, but it is not. (",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 18307,
                    "startIndex": 18263,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Probably Rubio told him this to convince him",
                      "textStyle": {
                        "backgroundColor": {
                          "color": {
                            "rgbColor": {
                              "blue": 0.91764706,
                              "green": 0.9137255,
                              "red": 0.90588236
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "endIndex": 18747,
                    "startIndex": 18307,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": ".) In the best case, $30bn in gross revenue a year for Venezuela (see thread-need to pay debt, interest, imports from that). Even if the US were to steal it all (impossible) it is a trivial sum of money for the US, 0.1% of GDP, more or less what NVIDIA generates in one quarter. This could never justify the huge political risk involved. You need to add that the US is now a net exporter, so it benefits from higher prices, not lower ones.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 18114
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 18748,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 18748,
                    "startIndex": 18747,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 18747
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 18809,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 18809,
                    "startIndex": 18748,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "^ This is subtweeting this by Brad Setser, CFR Senior Fellow\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 18748
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 18810,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 18810,
                    "startIndex": 18809,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 18809
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 19084,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 19084,
                    "startIndex": 18810,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Trump has indicated that he wants Venezuela to provide compensation—possibly tied to ICSID arbitration awards or even broader claims—for the past nationalization of U.S. assets. Such payments could consume a significant portion of the country's current oil export proceeds.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 18810
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 19085,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 19085,
                    "startIndex": 19084,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 19084
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 19385,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 19385,
                    "startIndex": 19085,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "It would not be entirely surprising if the administration also expects Venezuela to cover the costs of any new U.S. military bases in the region (pure speculation here), as it would likely prefer to avoid framing a new U.S. presence as a drain on American taxpayers—hardly an \"America First\" policy.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 19085
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 19386,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 19386,
                    "startIndex": 19385,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 19385
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 19643,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 19643,
                    "startIndex": 19386,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Venezuela, of course, carries a massive stock of unpaid debt: government bonds, PDVSA bonds, Chinese loans, and more. The principal on obvious claims alone exceeds $100 billion, with additional supplier credits and substantial accrued interest outstanding.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 19386
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 19644,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 19644,
                    "startIndex": 19643,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 19643
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 19819,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 19819,
                    "startIndex": 19644,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The chart referenced here comes from a 2019 paper by Richard Cooper and Mark Walker, two experienced sovereign debt lawyers. There are likely updated estimates available now.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 19644
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 19820,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 19820,
                    "startIndex": 19819,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 19819
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 20115,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 20115,
                    "startIndex": 19820,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The key point is that Venezuela's near-term oil revenue stream simply isn't large enough to cover rising imports (especially if the U.S. prioritizes stability), compensation for past expropriations and unpaid debts, and the substantial new investment required to significantly boost production.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 19820
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 20116,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 20116,
                    "startIndex": 20115,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 20115
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 20393,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 20393,
                    "startIndex": 20116,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "As Mark Sobel has observed, the standard approach in such cases would involve the IMF stepping in to assess external debts, establish credible figures, and determine the foreign exchange available for essential imports—framing the process in classic balance-of-payments terms.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 20116
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 20394,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 20394,
                    "startIndex": 20393,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 20393
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 20606,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 20606,
                    "startIndex": 20394,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "However, the IMF, as a multilateral institution, would not readily endorse a skewed arrangement prioritizing full payment to U.S. oil companies upfront while granting them preferential access to new concessions.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 20394
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 20607,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 20607,
                    "startIndex": 20606,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 20606
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 20785,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 20785,
                    "startIndex": 20607,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "It will be interesting to watch how the Trump administration navigates the constraints on Venezuela's oil export revenues and the reality of the country's severe cash shortages.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 20607
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 20786,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 20786,
                    "startIndex": 20785,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 20785
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 20788,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 20788,
                    "startIndex": 20786,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "-\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 20786
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 20789,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 20789,
                    "startIndex": 20788,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 20788
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 20804,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 20804,
                    "startIndex": 20789,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Niall Ferguson\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 20789
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 20805,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 20805,
                    "startIndex": 20804,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 20804
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 21041,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 21041,
                    "startIndex": 20805,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "The ejection of Maduro from Caracas is best understood as an invitation to turn the political clock back just over a century. The more I contemplate the contemporary scene, the more I think we have collectively accepted the invitation.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 20805
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 21042,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 21042,
                    "startIndex": 21041,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 21041
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 21313,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 21313,
                    "startIndex": 21042,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Foreign policy is just one area where we’re attempting to turn back time. Tariffs, the price of groceries, immigration restriction, antisemitism, socialism, corruption, vaccines, arms races: The issues of our time are issues our great-grandfathers debated 120 years ago.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 21042
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 21314,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 21314,
                    "startIndex": 21313,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 21313
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 21568,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 21568,
                    "startIndex": 21314,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "You may insist that the world of today is unrecognizably different from the world of, say, 1906 because technology has changed everything. To my eyes, the striking thing is how little difference all the new technology has made to the nature of politics.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 21314
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 21569,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 21569,
                    "startIndex": 21568,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 21568
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 21804,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 21804,
                    "startIndex": 21569,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "That the age of AI is more 19th-century than sci-fi was foreseen by Neal Stephenson in his dazzling masterpiece, The Diamond Age, where the inequalities created by new technology manifested themselves in a neo-Victorian elite culture.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 21569
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 21805,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 21805,
                    "startIndex": 21804,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 21804
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 21807,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 21807,
                    "startIndex": 21805,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "-\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 21805
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 21808,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 21808,
                    "startIndex": 21807,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 21807
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 22195,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 22195,
                    "startIndex": 21808,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "> Network token buybacks (I assume when just automatic, continuous) are not a controversial subject. The following is the argument for buybacks, which is supported by many big VCs and the prevailing wisdom. Note that Uniswap do buybacks with their revenues from the protocol (recently switched on). I will follow this with the argument against. These are, I think from 2025, resurfaced.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 21808
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 22196,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 22196,
                    "startIndex": 22195,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 22195
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 22208,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 22208,
                    "startIndex": 22196,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Jeff Dorman\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 22196
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 22209,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 22209,
                    "startIndex": 22208,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 22208
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 22287,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 22287,
                    "startIndex": 22209,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "This recent notion that token buybacks are a bad use of capital is misguided.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 22209
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 22288,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 22288,
                    "startIndex": 22287,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 22287
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 22484,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 22484,
                    "startIndex": 22288,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Token buybacks are by far the best use of capital for protocols, full stop.  Recent discussion against buybacks completely misses the biggest difference between tokens & equities, as I'll explain\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 22288
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 22485,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 22485,
                    "startIndex": 22484,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 22484
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 22576,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 22576,
                    "startIndex": 22485,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "1) First, hats off to the @MessariCrypto team for bringing this to light with actual data.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 22485
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 22577,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 22577,
                    "startIndex": 22576,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 22576
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 22698,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 22698,
                    "startIndex": 22577,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "But just because the buybacks, to date, have not led to token outperformance does NOT mean that it is the wrong strategy\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 22577
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 22699,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 22699,
                    "startIndex": 22698,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 22698
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 22976,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 22976,
                    "startIndex": 22699,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "2) The key difference between token & equity buybacks is that equity issuance is perpetual. There is no supply limit.  Stock is therefore outstanding forever & a company can always issue more.  So buying back stock is a trade, with the goal of buying low, & re-selling higher.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 22699
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 22977,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 22977,
                    "startIndex": 22976,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 22976
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 23148,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 23148,
                    "startIndex": 22977,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "3) Therefore, capital allocation decisions (buying back stock vs investing in growth) is a more important decision for a company.  You really are trying to create an ROI.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 22977
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 23149,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 23149,
                    "startIndex": 23148,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 23148
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 23396,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 23396,
                    "startIndex": 23149,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "4) Tokens have a fixed supply, & the protocol has no ability to be \"acquired\" in the end state.  So the buyback matters a lot more. Every stakeholder owns it (founding team, employees, customers, passive investors), and benefits from the buyback.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 23149
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 23397,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 23397,
                    "startIndex": 23396,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 23396
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 23600,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 23600,
                    "startIndex": 23397,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "5) Moreover, there’s often no reason why the token has to exist beyond initial bootstrapping phase. They can amortize it down to 0 tokens outstanding over a long period of time & every stakeholder wins.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 23397
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 23601,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 23601,
                    "startIndex": 23600,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 23600
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 23787,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 23787,
                    "startIndex": 23601,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "6)  Look at $LEO.  It's a company, w/ common equity, but also has a token which is amortizing daily, & may ultimately go away completely when Bitfinex gets the money back from the hack.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 23601
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 23788,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 23788,
                    "startIndex": 23787,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 23787
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 23921,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 23921,
                    "startIndex": 23788,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "^ Then here’s the argument against indiscriminate buybacks, first by this random and then by David, Head of Advisory for Blockworks.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
                }
              },
              "startIndex": 23788
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 23922,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 23922,
                    "startIndex": 23921,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "\n",
