                      "content": "^ Posted by Michael Burry, it shows expensive stocks relative to ancient history. The interesting thing with this chart is that after the dotcom rise, stocks have been permanently at least at the high end of historic valuations. The 2008 crash takes the index down to only the average valuation from the period before the web and broadband internet. This feels to me like technology valuations are simply higher and that has been fine. Post AI, this may see another reset. Someone else points out Sarbanes Oxley, 2002. Others point to money printing.\n",
