                }
              },
              "startIndex": 173597
            },
            {
              "endIndex": 174508,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "endIndex": 174508,
                    "startIndex": 173598,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "> I sold my Bitcoin today. I have stopped truly believing in the face of the gold and silver rallies. The narrative pushing gold higher was supposed to be the one that pushes Bitcoin to the extremes. That has not happened and shows that people just don’t see it, probably because of a number of things. There’s worry over quantum computing, and solving it may require changes to the Bitcoin code (to protect or move people’s assets) which shows just how the immutable properties of Bitcoin are just in mutable code. Also, there is a massive opportunity cost to owning it in the AI era, since there is money to be made in genuinely productive stocks. Finally, if you want a store of value, stocks are good but also gold-backed ERC20s can be sent around. Bitcoin looks like an also-ran. Meanwhile gold is entering its wild toppy volatility stage. I’m worried that bubble bursting might bring general negativity.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT"
